313
00:20:17.972 --> 00:20:21.682
degradation over time, meaning it won't produce as much

314
00:20:21.712 --> 00:20:24.311
power as it would at the beginning of its life.

315
00:20:25.892 --> 00:20:27.372
Then there are single event effects.

316
00:20:28.252 --> 00:20:31.492
Probably the most well-known of them is the single event upsets,

317
00:20:32.092 --> 00:20:35.872
which are bit flips caused by a single heavily ionized particle

318
00:20:35.972 --> 00:20:39.952
passing through a transistor, which induces a charge large enough to

319
00:20:40.032 --> 00:20:42.292
change the state of the node from a one to a zero,

320
00:20:43.592 --> 00:20:45.072
or a zero to a one, depending.

321
00:20:46.812 --> 00:20:50.772
Then there are single event transients, which are brief glitches in performance,

322
00:20:50.812 --> 00:20:52.012
such as voltage spikes.

323
00:20:52.972 --> 00:20:56.112
Then there are single event latch ups, which are parasitic loops

324
00:20:56.332 --> 00:20:56.972
generating

325
00:20:57.852 --> 00:21:01.172
a low impedance path in the transistor between power and ground.

326
00:21:02.032 --> 00:21:03.712
And this can be fixed by power cycling.

327
00:21:04.592 --> 00:21:08.512
Then there's single event burnout, which is the destruction of a device

328
00:21:08.552 --> 00:21:12.532
due to high voltage that exceeds the breakdown voltage of the transistor, which

329
00:21:12.552 --> 00:21:13.752
results in permanent failure.

330
00:21:14.592 --> 00:21:16.422
Then there are single event gate ruptures,

331
00:21:17.292 --> 00:21:21.012
which is the formation of a conducting path in the gate oxide, which you can

332
00:21:21.072 --> 00:21:23.772
see demonstrated by this image here.

333
00:21:25.772 --> 00:21:28.152
Then there are some mitigation approaches

334
00:21:29.072 --> 00:21:32.772
to prevent these. One of the simplest ones would be to add

335
00:21:32.832 --> 00:21:33.352
shielding.

336
00:21:34.432 --> 00:21:38.352
This is very useful for stopping lower energy particles and is generally a

337
00:21:38.372 --> 00:21:40.932
good method for reducing the total ionizing dose.

338
00:21:41.912 --> 00:21:45.692
As you can see by this image here, there's another similar one in

339
00:21:45.772 --> 00:21:49.632
the Tribble textbook that basically just highlights the

